n": "We are given the equation:\n\n$$\n(x - 3)^3 + (x - 7)^3 = (2x - 10)^3\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Expand both sides\n\nLet\u2019s expand the left-hand side (LHS) and the right-hand side (RHS).\n\n#### Left-Hand Side (LHS):\n\n$$\n(x - 3)^3 + (x - 7)^3\n$$\n\nUse the binomial expansion:\n\n$$\n(x - a)^3 = x^3 - 3a x^2 + 3a^2 x - a^3\n$$\n\nSo:\n\n- $(x - 3)^3 = x^3 - 9x^2 + 27x - 27$\n- $(x - 7)^3 = x^3 - 21x^2 + 147x - 343$\n\nAdd them:\n\n$$\n(x - 3)^3 + (x - 7)^3 = (x^3 - 9x^2 + 27x - 27) + (x^3 - 21x^2 + 147x - 343)\n$$\n\n$$\n= 2x^3 - 30x^2 + 174x - 370\n$$\n\n#### Right-Hand Side (RHS):\n\n$$\n(2x - 10)^3\n$$\n\nUse the binomial expansion again:\n\n$$\n(2x - 10)^3 = (2x)^3 - 3(2x)^2(10) + 3(2x)(10)^2 - (10)^3\n$$\n\n$$\n= 8x^3 - 120x^2 + 600x - 1000\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Set both sides equal\n\n$$\n2x^3 - 30x^2 + 174x - 370 = 8x^3 - 120x^2 + 600x - 1000\n$$\n\nBring all terms to one side:\n\n$$\n0 = 8x^3 - 120x^2 + 600x - 1000 - (2x^3 - 30x^2 + 174x - 370)\n$$\n\n$$\n= 8x^3 - 120x^2 + 600x - 1000 - 2x^3 + 30x^2 - 174x + 370\n$$\n\n$$\n= (8x^3 - 2x^3) + (-120x^2 + 30x^2) + (600x - 174x) + (-1000 + 370)\n$$\n\n$$\n= 6x^3 - 90x^2 + 426x - 630\n$$\n\nSo the equation becomes:\n\n$$\n6x^3 - 90x^2 + 426x - 630 = 0\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Simplify the equation\n\nDivide the entire equation by 6:\n\n$$\nx^3 - 15x^2 + 71x - 105 = 0\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 4: Solve the cubic equation\n\nWe now solve:\n\n$$\nx^3 - 15x^2 + 71x - 105 = 0\n$$\n\nTry rational root theorem: possible rational roots are factors of 105 over 1, i.e., \u00b11, \u00b13, \u00b15, \u00b17, \u00b115, \u00b121, \u00b135, \u00b1105.\n\nTry $x = 3$:\n\n$$\n3^3 - 15(3)^2 + 71(3) - 105 = 27 - 135 + 213 - 105 = 0\n$$\n\nSo $x = 3$ is a root.\n\nNow perform polynomial division or factor out $(x - 3)$.\n\nUse synthetic division:\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{r|rrrr}\n3 & 1 & -15 & 71 & -105 \\\\\n  &   &  3  & -36 & 105 \\\\\n\\hline\n  & 1 & -12 & 35  &  0 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n$$\n\nSo the cubic factors as:\n\n$$\n(x - 3)(x^2 - 12x + 35) = 0\n$$\n\nNow solve the quadratic:\n\n$$\nx^2 - 12x + 35 = 0\n$$\n\nUse the quadratic formula:\n\n$$\nx = \\frac{12 \\pm \\sqrt{(-12)^2 - 4(1)(35)}}{2} = \\frac{12 \\pm \\sqrt{144 - 140}}{2} = \\frac{12 \\pm \\sqrt{4}}{2}\n$$\n\n$$\nx = \\frac{12 \\pm 2}{2} = 7 \\text{ or } 5\n$$\n\n---\n\n### \u2705 Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{3, 5, 7}\n$$\n\nThese are the roots of the equation.", "diagnostic_seconds": 31.55986478831619}
