the pentagon by a certain angle, it will look the same as before.\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Determine the angle of rotation\n\nTo find the **minimum angle of rotation** that maps the pentagon onto itself, we divide the full circle (360\u00b0) by the number of sides (or equivalently, the number of rotational symmetries):\n\n$$\n\\text{Minimum rotation angle} = \\frac{360^\\circ}{5} = 72^\\circ\n$$\n\n---\n\n### \u2705 Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{72^\\circ}\n$$\n\nSo, the **minimum number of degrees** the pentagon must be rotated counterclockwise about its center to coincide with its original position is **72 degrees**.", "diagnostic_seconds": 6.689030805137008}
